{"toolCallId":"call_fddf0de2211a4963b8545a85ab3bf165","title":"Wrote ./specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8a66e200e3/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path)\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.3 -->\n# Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n<!-- FILL: Keep the prefix table and add the two shell variables this task list uses. GOOD: `S` is the script path. `P` is the packet path. WEAK: Variables are defined below. -->\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n<!-- FILL: Replace the sample tasks with the real setup steps. Each task names a file and a verify command. GOOD: T001 Read the output block in `recommend-level.sh`. Verify: `rg -n 'Recommended Level'` prints one line. WEAK: T001 Set up the project. -->\n\n- [ ] T001 Create project structure\n- [ ] T002 Install dependencies\n- [ ] T003 [P] Configure development tools\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n<!-- FILL: Write one implementation task per file change. Add a `Verify:` line with the command and its expected output. GOOD: T002 Add the `--quiet` branch. Verify: `--quiet` prints one line. WEAK: T002 Implement the feature. -->\n\n- [ ] T004 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Implement core feature 1]\n- [ ] T005 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Implement core feature 2]\n- [ ] T006 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Implement core feature 3]\n- [ ] T007 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Add error handling]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n<!-- FILL: Write one verification task per requirement. Each one runs a command. GOOD: T003 Run both invocations. Verify: `wc -l` prints 1 and 17. WEAK: T003 Test everything. -->\n\n- [ ] T008 Test happy path manually\n- [ ] T009 Test edge cases\n- [ ] T010 Update documentation\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n<!-- FILL: Keep the three completion lines and add the one artifact that proves the phase is done. GOOD: `--quiet` prints one line and the suite passes. WEAK: Work is complete. -->\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n<!-- FILL: Name the spec and plan files. Add the decision record when the packet has one. GOOD: Specification: `spec.md`. Plan: `plan.md`. WEAK: See the other docs. -->\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n\n\n\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.3 -->\n# Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n\n**Shell variables** used below:\n\n| Variable | Value |\n|----------|-------|\n| `$S` | `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh` |\n| `$F` | A fixture spec folder with at least one unfilled placeholder |\n| `$P` | The percentage the run prints, read before the comparison: `P=$(bash $S $F \\| sed -n 's/.*Overall Completion: \\([0-9]*\\)%.*/\\1/p')` |\n\nExport `S` and `F` before running a verify command. `P` is read from the run itself, so no fixture needs an exact percentage.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Record the current report and exit status for the fixture folder (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S $F; echo \"exit=$?\"` prints the report and `exit=0`.\n- [ ] T002 Read the option loop and the trailing `exit 0` (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n 'exit 0|--file\\|-f' $S` prints the parser case and the final `exit 0`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T003 Add a `MIN_PERCENT` global beside `SINGLE_FILE`, empty by default (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n '^MIN_PERCENT=' $S` prints one line.\n- [ ] T004 Parse `--min-percent <N>` in the option loop and reject a missing value with exit 1 (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --min-percent` prints `ERROR:` on stderr and `echo \"exit=$?\"` prints `exit=1`.\n- [ ] T005 Reject a non-integer or out-of-range N with exit 1 and an `ERROR:` line on stderr (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --min-percent 101 $F` prints `ERROR:` on stderr and `echo \"exit=$?\"` prints `exit=1`.\n- [ ] T006 Compare the printed percentage with N after the output call and exit 3 when it is below (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --min-percent $((P+1)) $F; echo \"exit=$?\"` prints `exit=3`.\n- [ ] T007 Add the option to the `show_help()` block (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --help | rg -- '--min-percent <N>'` prints one line.\n- [ ] T008 Record exit code 3 in the trailing exit-code comment (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n '^#   3' $S` prints one line.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T009 Prove the report is unchanged with the option present (`$S`). Verify: `diff <(bash $S $F) <(bash $S --min-percent 0 $F)` prints nothing.\n- [ ] T010 Prove both threshold outcomes against the same run (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --min-percent $P $F; echo \"exit=$?\"` prints `exit=0`, and `bash $S --min-percent $((P+1)) $F; echo \"exit=$?\"` prints `exit=3`.\n- [ ] T011 Prove `--file` mode applies the floor to the file's own completion (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --file $F/spec.md --min-percent 100; echo \"exit=$?\"` prints `exit=0` for a file with no placeholders.\n- [ ] T012 Re-run strict validation on this packet (`specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent`). Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent --strict | tail -1` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n- [ ] The `diff` of the reports with and without `--min-percent` is empty, and both exit statuses 0 and 3 were observed\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":24,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":20}}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8a66e200e3/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"write"}}
